Local development fork addendum
This fork imports and adapts MiaAI-Lab's GLM-5.3-Flash recipe and native
arithmetic, and ports the GLM spill tier by Robert Wojciechowski (wojo).
Copyright 2026 MiaAI-Lab. The donor's Apache-2.0 LICENSE, NOTICE and CREDITS
are retained unmodified in LICENSES/donors/mia-f1ee79a6/. The later full-target
graph port adapts production segmented KDA orchestration and the GLM metadata/
owner protocol; its original production-lineage notices are retained unmodified
in LICENSES/donors/mia-b5808ac6/ and LICENSES/donors/wojo-7fac72b3/.
Original and transitive credits, immutable source references, and local changes
are described in LICENSES/donors/README.md. Those credits supplement, and do
not replace, the upstream and third-party notices above.

The GLM prompt latent AOT integration embeds unmodified production TensorFold
Triton sparse-onepass and BF16 absorb/expand kernels. Local changes provide
native ownership, validation, prompt dispatch and numerical/cache identity.
Their exact source/image/compiler/payload provenance and retained original
license are in zig/src/families/glm/prompt_aot/; the Mia and wojo lineage and
transitive credits above remain applicable.

The Qwen CUDA text operations and host mathematical references adapt work
Copyright 2025 The Qwen Team and The HuggingFace Inc. team, under Apache-2.0.
The original license and exact source revision are retained in
LICENSES/donors/transformers-e0eb2810/ and LICENSES/donors/README.md.

The Clef CPU checkpoint inspector retains Cloudflare's unmodified Clef Flash
configuration, safetensors index and JSON shard headers, based on
Qwen/Qwen3.5-9B. Its pinned source, hashes and capture scope are recorded beside
the fixtures. Cloudflare's original Apache-2.0 license and model card are
retained in LICENSES/donors/clef-flash-fde727a2/. Local changes add strict BF16
metadata admission, allocation planning, mapped payload ownership, host row
gathers, loading through shared Qwen projection components and request-owned
hidden output from the shared backbone. An explicit development-only dense
initializer adds bounded host embedding staging and separate terminal weights.
Native serving remains disabled. No checkpoint weights or Clef model
implementation are included.

The native Clef library in zig/src/families/clef/ and include/tfclef.h adapts
the design of Cloudflare's clef-flash joint_schema_model.py (Apache-2.0,
revision fde727a287004204b7518dcc983fe64379776712): the joint schema head's
tensor roles and the encoded record's spans. It is a reimplementation; no
Cloudflare code is copied into Zig, C or CUDA. Its fixtures retain Cloudflare's
unmodified joint_head_config.json and joint_head.safetensors JSON header, with
their hashes in zig/src/families/clef/fixtures/capture.json.
